# Rule: unknown_mcp_server
# Category: MCP Supply Chain
# Severity: high
# Attack Class: supply_chain
#
# Detects tool calls using the MCP (Model Context Protocol) where the
# tool name is NOT in the approved per-environment allowlist.
# MCP servers can execute arbitrary code, read files, and make network
# calls — a compromised or rogue MCP server is a critical risk.
#
# The allowlist "approved_mcp_tools" is configured at engine startup.
# If the allowlist is empty/unconfigured, the allowlist check is a no-op
# and only the heuristic regex decides.
#
# Two-layer defence:
#   1. Always: require tool name matching code-execution patterns
#   2. If allowlist exists: also exclude explicitly approved tools

event.type == "TOOL_CALL"
AND event.raw_data.protocol == "mcp"
AND regex_match("(?i)(exec|shell|bash|cmd|system|eval|subprocess|os\\.run|command|execute|terminal|run_code|code_interpreter)", event.raw_data.tool_name)
AND NOT in_allowlist(event.raw_data.tool_name, "approved_mcp_tools")
